## Test of habitat x pathway composition (aliens < 10 pooled: Coniferous,
Broad-leaved, Scrublands, Rock outcrops)
Chi-square pooled: chi2=66.20, df=12, p=1.6e-09 (min expected 0.62 < 5, so
chi-square is only indicative) -> permutation test, 20,000 shuffles with
row/column totals fixed: p=5.0e-05. Composition differs strongly across habitats.

## Supporting context (not merged with plot data)
- invasion_success_pathways.csv (81 species): Gardening 42 (52%), Unintentional
  30, AgriForest 9. No per-species habitat column -> species-level habitat
  attribution NOT possible from these files. Phylo linkage OK (76/81 tips match).
- temporal_trends_contingency_table.csv (regional first records): gardening
  share rises 17% (Before 1500) -> 75% (1985-2019); count 18 -> 397.

## Caveats
- n.* counting semantics (distinct species vs occurrences; possible multi-
  pathway assignment of one species within a plot) undocumented.
- 441 zero-aliens plots treated as true absences.
- Low-evidence habitats (<=9 alien records) not used for the primary claim.
